# libretranslate
msgid "A role that declares no users contributes none, so the result follows the deployment rather than everything the repository could ever deploy. Two roles sharing a user must agree on its policy: the account is one thing, so silently picking one declaration would hand the other role a password its application rejects."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A role that declares none takes the run's whole pool, which is what spreads both architectures evenly over its variants: every row of the catalogue advances the same rotation, so a role's consecutive rows alternate rather than repeating one architecture."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A role that gains a `shared_net` overlay changes its network layout: the project's default network, named after the entity and carrying the declared local subnet, is replaced by an unnamed project default, and the entity name passes to an externally managed network. Docker cannot relabel an existing network, so on a deployment that already ran, the network has to be recreated, and that fails while any consumer holds an endpoint on it:"
msgstr "그 역할은 `shared_net` 오버레이는 네트워크 레이아웃을 변경합니다. 이 프로젝트의 기본 네트워크는, 엔티티티티가되고 선언 된 로컬 서브넷을 운반 한 후, 이름이 아닌 프로젝트 기본으로 대체되며, 엔티티티 이름은 외부 관리 네트워크로 전달됩니다. Docker는 기존 네트워크를 다시 표시할 수 없으므로 이미 랜을 배포하는 경우 네트워크가 재창조되고 소비자가 최종 지점을 보유하고있는 동안 실패합니다."

msgid "A role that hands ``sys-pip-install`` a bare package name follows whatever pip resolves; one that pins ``name==version`` freezes it, and nothing thaws it again. The docker updater keeps image tags current and dependabot reads ``pyproject.toml``; neither sees a version inside an Ansible task variable, so a pin set once ages silently."
msgstr ""

msgid "A role that only one architecture can run declares it on its primary service entity, next to `modes`:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A role usually owns one capability:"
msgstr ""

msgid "A role whose own asserts need something the dependency closure does not supply (a served model, a second backend) carries them here, because ``--include`` filters the generated inventory to the ids it is given literally: a provider pulled in as a dependency runs, but never joins ``group_names``, so a flag gated on that stays false and the deploy the README documents stops on the assert."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A role whose upstream images are amd64-only must say so in `meta/services.yml`, or half its rows fail on the image pull. That failure is loud and names the role, which is the intended way to discover the gap."
msgstr "업스트림 이미지가 amd의 역할64-만 그렇게 말해야 `meta/services.yml`, 또는 절반 그것의 줄은 이미지 잡아당기기에 실패합니다. 그 실패는 좁고 역할 이름을 붙이고, 이는 틈을 발견 할 수있는 의도 된 방법입니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A role with few rows would never leave its first architecture, and per-role spread is the point of the axis."
msgstr "몇 줄의 역할은 첫 번째 아키텍처를 결코 떠나지 않을 것입니다, per-role 스프레드는 축의 포인트입니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A role's `meta/services.yml` MAY contain (per-service-entity):"
msgstr "역할의 `meta/services.yml` MAY 포함 (고객 지원)::"

# libretranslate
msgid "A role's entry for its own entity is skipped: a role does not bond to itself, and those entries carry unrelated topics such as users or domains."
msgstr "자신의 법인에 대한 역할의 항목은 건너뛰고 있습니다 : 역할은 자체에 접착되지 않으며 그 항목은 사용자 또는 도메인과 같은 관련 주제를 수행합니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A role's lifecycle value sits on a single linear axis from `planned` (no code yet) to `eol` (end of life). A subset of stages is the **tested** envelope: roles in those stages MUST be exercised by the project's automated test suite on every change, and a failing test blocks the release. Stages outside that envelope MAY ship without automated coverage."
msgstr "역할의 수명주기 값은 단일 선형 축에 앉아 `planned` (아직 코드 없음) 으로 `eol` (삶의 끝). 단계의 subset는 입니다 **테스트** envelope: 이 단계의 역할은 프로젝트의 자동화 테스트 제품군에 의해 수행되고, 실패 테스트는 릴리스를 차단합니다. 자동화된 적용 없이 봉투 MAY 배 밖에 단계."

# libretranslate
msgid "A role's task that reads its own service flag therefore picks up the runtime-resolved value, even when the inventory carried a Jinja string for that flag: the conditional evaluates against the play's actual `group_names`, which reflects which other application groups the host joined."
msgstr "자신의 서비스 플래그를 읽는 역할의 작업은 따라서 런타임 해결 된 값을 선택, 심지어 재고가 그 플래그에 대한 Jinja 문자열을 수행 할 때: 조건은 플레이의 실제에 대한 평가 `group_names`, 다른 응용 프로그램 그룹이 호스트에 합류하는 것을 반영합니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A round deploys a provider once, so the role that pulls it in is the only place that can say how lean it has to be. A variant entry may therefore carry any application config topic under the service it depends on:"
msgstr "라운드는 공급자를 한 번 배치, 그래서 그것에 끌어 당기는 역할은 그것이 될 수 있다는 것을 말할 수있는 유일한 장소입니다. 변형 항목은 따라서 서비스에 따라 애플리케이션 구성 항목을 수행 할 수 있습니다."

msgid "A round picks one variant per role, and that choice decides two things no single role's `meta/services.yml` can state on its own: which providers the role still pulls in, and how lean those providers have to be (:mod:`utils.roles.applications.topics`). Both are resolved here, so the matrix planner's include set, the inventory bake and the CI selection read one answer instead of three."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A row several tokens name is emitted once per token, which is the whole point of the axes: ``role#1@compose+tor role#1@swarm+tor`` is one variant that failed in two modes, and it has to come back as two deploys. Two tokens narrowing a row the same way collapse into one, so a duplicate in the input cannot become two jobs racing for one artifact name."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A row the priority line claims is never the answer. ``regular`` is discovered without the priority line (see the retrigger's ``_ranking``), so it still holds rows the run will hand to that line instead (:func:`cli.meta.ci.matrix.candidates`): a variant-less pin takes its whole role, a pinned one takes those variants. Naming such a row would emit an offset that resolves against nothing once the run applies the priority line, and abort the discovery of every chunk."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A row's position is its index in the uncapped discovery order, not its index inside a chunk, so slicing the list into chunks never changes what a row is assigned. A priority row, which deploys several mode/tor combinations at once, walks the distro and filesystem rotations across those combinations rather than repeating one pair."
msgstr "행의 위치는 uncapped discovery 순서에 있는 그것의 색인입니다, 펑크 안쪽에 그것의 색인, 그래서 slicing the list into chunks never changes what a row is 할당된. 한 번에 여러 모드 / 토르 조합을 배치하는 우선 순위 행, 한 쌍을 반복하는 것보다 그 조합을 통해 디트로 및 파일 시스템 교체를 걸어."

# libretranslate
msgid "A run that names a kind to chase a filesystem-dependent path could go green on a different one."
msgstr "파일 시스템 의존 경로가 서로 녹색으로 갈 수 있다는 것을 의미한다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A run that permits two or more kinds is a preference, not a demand. The matrix has already narrowed each row to one kind out of that pool, so falling back to another kind the run allowed stays inside what the operator asked for, while failing the row does not. A run whose whole permitted pool is unservable fails rather than leaving the pool."
msgstr ""

msgid "A run the source carries itself is left alone, because an aligned block in a code sample means its spacing."
msgstr ""

msgid "A run-wide choice cannot cover them. Five distributions and three filesystems are fifteen combinations, and a sweep that fixes one pair for all of its rows would need fifteen sweeps to say anything about the rest, while reporting green the whole time."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A same-size swapfile helps absorb memory spikes on Linux. On Windows and macOS, you SHOULD keep enough free disk space available for virtual memory and local caches."
msgstr "동일한 크기의 swapfile은 Linux에서 메모리 스파이크를 흡수합니다. Windows 및 macOS에서 SHOULD는 가상 메모리 및 로컬 캐시에 사용할 수있는 충분한 무료 디스크 공간을 유지합니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A sample whose install failed is recorded as ``None`` and ranks worse than any duration, so an outage counts fully rather than being dropped."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled differential backup of the NFS export onto the local backup directory. Each run stores a discrete snapshot under `<backups>/<machine-hash>/backup-nfs-to-local/<generation>/files/`, hard-linked against the previous generation via rsync `--link-dest`."
msgstr "로컬 백업 디렉토리에 NFS 수출의 예정된 차별 백업. 각 런은 분리된 스냅샷을 저장합니다. `<backups>/<machine-hash>/backup-nfs-to-local/<generation>/files/`, rsync를 통해 이전 세대에 대한 하드 링크 `--link-dest`·."

# libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled differential backup of the NFS export onto the local backup directory. Each run stores a discrete snapshot under ``<backups>/<machine-hash>/backup-nfs-to-local/<generation>/files/``, hard-linked against the previous generation via rsync ``--link-dest``."
msgstr "로컬 백업 디렉토리에 NFS 수출의 예정된 차별 백업. 각 런은 분리된 스냅샷을 저장합니다. ``<backups>/<machine-hash>/backup-nfs-to-local/<generation>/files/``, rsync를 통해 이전 세대에 대한 하드 링크 ``--link-dest``·."

# libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled pull-style backup that replicates the backup trees of one or more remote provider hosts onto this host via SSH + rsync. The receiving side is the trust anchor: each retrieval is a discrete snapshot, hard-linked against the previous one, with a retry loop guarding against transient network failures."
msgstr "SSH + rsync를 통해이 호스트에 하나 이상의 원격 공급자 호스트의 백업 나무를 복제하는 예정된 풀 스타일 백업. 수신 측은 신뢰 닻입니다: 각 retrieval는 전진한 네트워크 실패에 대하여 retry 반복 감시와 더불어 전진한 것에 대하여 단단한 연결되는 분리된 스냅샷입니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled workflow (`cron-*.yml`) drops the `Category:` schema: its `name:` MUST read as one short sentence saying what the run does, because the Actions list shows scheduled runs next to each other with no PR or branch to tell them apart."
msgstr "계획된 워크플로우 (`cron-*.yml`) 자주 묻는 질문 `Category:` schema: 그것의 `name:` MUST는 하나의 짧은 문장이 실행하는 것을 말하는 것과 같이 읽습니다. Actions list는 PR 또는 Branch와 같은 각 다른 실행을 표시하기 때문에 출발을 알려줍니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled, deduplicating backup of every Docker container's data on this host to a local backup directory. File payloads are captured with rsync hard-link snapshots; databases register themselves into a central seed file so each backup run also dumps a consistent SQL snapshot via [baudolo](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/backup-docker-to-local)."
msgstr "이 호스트의 모든 Docker 컨테이너의 데이터를 로컬 백업 디렉토리에 deduplicating 백업. 파일 페이로드는 rsync hard-link snapshots로 캡처됩니다. 데이터베이스는 중앙 씨 파일로 자신을 등록하므로 각 백업은 일관된 SQL 스냅 샷을 덤프합니다. [뚱 베어](https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/backup-docker-to-local)·."

# libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled, deduplicating backup of every Docker container’s data on this host to a local backup directory. File payloads are captured with rsync hard-link snapshots; databases register themselves into a central seed file so each backup run also dumps a consistent SQL snapshot via `baudolo <https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/backup-docker-to-local>`__."
msgstr "이 호스트의 모든 Docker 컨테이너의 데이터를 로컬 백업 디렉토리에 deduplicating 백업. 파일 페이로드는 rsync hard-link snapshots로 캡처됩니다. 데이터베이스는 중앙 씨 파일로 자신을 등록하므로 각 백업은 일관된 SQL 스냅 샷을 덤프합니다. `baudolo <https://github.com/kevinveenbirkenbach/backup-docker-to-local>`__·."

# libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled, deduplicating backup of the host's generated secret material to the local backup directory: the Infinito.Nexus secrets and tokens, the self-signed root CA, the Let's Encrypt account + certificates, the ACME DNS credentials, and the node identity (ssh host keys + machine-id). None of this lives in a docker volume, the NFS export or the operator inventory, so it is the gap the volume/nfs backup roles do not cover."
msgstr "호스트의 생성된 비밀 자료를 로컬 백업 디렉토리에 deduplicating 백업: Infinito.Nexus 비밀과 토큰, 자기 서명 루트 CA, Let's Encrypt 계정 + 인증서, ACME DNS 자격 증명 및 노드 ID (ssh 주인 열쇠 + 기계 ID). 이 생활의 아무도는 도커 양, NFS 수출 또는 통신수 재고에서, 그래서 그것입니다 부피/nfs 백업 역할은 커버하지 않습니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A scheduled, deduplicating backup of the host’s generated secret material to the local backup directory: the Infinito.Nexus secrets and tokens, the self-signed root CA, the Let’s Encrypt account + certificates, the ACME DNS credentials, and the node identity (ssh host keys + machine-id). None of this lives in a docker volume, the NFS export or the operator inventory, so it is the gap the volume/nfs backup roles do not cover."
msgstr "호스트의 생성된 비밀 자료를 로컬 백업 디렉토리에 deduplicating 백업: Infinito.Nexus 비밀과 토큰, 자체 서명 루트 CA, Let’s Encrypt 계정 + 인증서, ACME DNS 자격 증명, 노드 ID (ssh 주인 열쇠 + 기계 ID). 이 생활의 아무도는 도커 양, NFS 수출 또는 통신수 재고에서, 그래서 그것입니다 부피/nfs 백업 역할은 커버하지 않습니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A script in this directory MUST work across every distro variant that the runner image is built for (currently Debian, Ubuntu, Arch, Fedora, CentOS). Tool availability differs across these variants, so a script SHOULD branch on `command -v <tool>` rather than on distro IDs."
msgstr "이 디렉토리의 스크립트는 런너 이미지가 내장된 모든 디트로 변종을 통해 MUST 작업 (현재 Debian, Ubuntu, Arch, Fedora, CentOS). 도구 가용성은 이러한 변형에 따라 다릅니다, 그래서 스크립트 SHOULD 지점 `command -v <tool>` 디트로 ID보다."

msgid "A script that is bind-mounted from this directory into a fixed in-container path (see [compose.yml](../../compose.yml)) MUST keep its git executable bit, because Docker bind-mounts preserve host file permissions and the in-container caller (systemd, dockerd, the entrypoint) cannot recover from a non-executable mount."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A second tag next to every image, which the registry cleanup then has to protect as children of the plain tag. Pushing by digest gives the same manifest list without it."
msgstr ""

msgid "A secret denylist such as `grep -v 'password|token|key'` does **NOT** count as protection: it is case-sensitive, and secrets also travel inside URL paths. Local deploys run with `MASK_CREDENTIALS_IN_LOGS` disabled, so `no_log` does not mask these tasks."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A selection token names a role and MAY narrow the axes that role's rows would otherwise be assigned: which variants run, which deploy mode, whether the row goes behind the node onion, which distribution it deploys on, which filesystem its docker data root runs on and which CPU architecture it lands on. What a token leaves open stays open, exactly as an unpinned run leaves it: the priority line covers every mode and onion state the row can take, and the sweep rotation picks the distro, the filesystem and the architecture on both lines."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A selection token names a row that has to exist *on this branch* (:mod:`utils.github.variant.selection`). Nothing else in the chain can tell the operator that early: the matrix builder raises on the first bad token, one per chunk job, so a stale list costs one full CI round per entry and reports the second problem only after the first is fixed. Every problem is collected here instead, and the exit code gates the run."
msgstr "선택 토큰은 존재하는 행을 명함 *이 지점에서* (:mod:`utils.github.variant.selection`). 체인의 다른 점은 초기 연산자를 말할 수 없습니다 : 첫 번째 나쁜 토큰에 매트릭스 빌더, 펑크 일 당 하나, 그래서 stale 목록은 항목 당 하나의 전체 CI 라운드를 요하고 첫 번째가 고정 된 후 두 번째 문제를보고. 모든 문제는 여기에 수집되며, 종료 코드 게이트가 실행됩니다."

msgid "A server that loses its way answers ``Cloud`` with ``Cloud Cloud Cloud``. Every other rule passes it: the spans survive, the markup count survives, it is no echo, and ``truncated`` only watches the short side."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A service is a reusable dependency that an application enables via `services.<service_key>`."
msgstr "이 서비스는 애플리케이션이 활성화되도록 재사용 가능한 의존성입니다. `services.<service_key>`·."

# libretranslate
msgid "A service key is group-conditional when some role declares it with a Jinja ``enabled`` expression rather than a literal, i.e. the shape ``tests/integration/roles/meta/services/test_dynamic_flags.py`` enforces. Those keys are the ones a test deploy may drop without changing what the role under test is: their providers are co-deployed only because a host happens to be in the provider's group."
msgstr "몇몇 역할이 Jinja로 선언할 때 서비스 열쇠는 그룹 상태입니다 ``enabled`` 리터럴보다는 표현식, 즉, 모양 ``tests/integration/roles/meta/services/test_dynamic_flags.py`` 법적 고지 이러한 키는 테스트 배포판이 테스트 아래 역할을 변경하지 않고 드롭 할 수 있습니다 : 호스트가 공급자의 그룹에있기 때문에 해당 공급자는 공동 배포됩니다."

# libretranslate
msgid "A service that spells its probe out instead of picking a flavor."
msgstr "맛 대신 프로브를 판매하는 서비스."

msgid "A services.<key> flag (``enabled`` / ``shared``) MAY be true if it is the literal Python ``True``, any string containing the substring ``in group_names``, or a string referencing a `GROUP_GATED_CONSTANTS` entry. Negated and compound predicates (``\"{{ 'X' not in group_names }}\"``) match on purpose: they are true on some node shape, and the static closure is the co-deploy superset. Mirrors the substring test at ``tests/integration/roles/meta/services/test_dynamic_flags.py:194``."
msgstr ""

msgid "A shared infrastructure network carries lateral reach between the applications that join it, so `allowed_consumers` is an application-layer decision the network does not enforce. Measured on the compose stack: Flowise and Baserow both join `postgres` because both use the central database, and Flowise opens `baserow:80` at `192.168.200.5` although Baserow does not admit Flowise as a consumer. A client whose users can name a URL is bounded only by its deny list, which covers loopback, link-local metadata and multicast but no application host. Reach MUST be measured by resolved address, never by name: an unknown name falls through to a wildcard resolver that answers with one reachable address, so a name-based probe reports every peer as reachable and proves nothing. Bounding lateral reach needs a network policy or per-pair networks rather than the current shared-service topology."
msgstr ""

msgid "A shared mapper that imports every LDAP group with `preserve.group.inheritance=true` MUST NOT be used. Role names recur across applications (`administrator`, `editor`, ...) and Keycloak's `GroupTreeResolver` keys its lookup map on the group name, so the second `administrator` silently overwrites the first."
msgstr ""

msgid "A short paragraph that describes what the **role** does: what it deploys, configures, and integrates. Reference any companion documentation files (e.g. `Administration.md`) here using file-name link text."
msgstr ""

msgid "A short paragraph that describes what the **software** is. You MUST NOT describe what the role does here. Link the software name to its official website on first use."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A sidecar ``web-app-keycloak`` oauth2-proxy authenticates the visitor against Keycloak (OIDC, or LDAP federated through Keycloak) and nginx overwrites the ``X-Forwarded-*`` identity headers on every proxied request."
msgstr "사이드카 ``web-app-keycloak`` 오우즈2-proxy는 방문자에게 Keycloak (OIDC, 또는 LDAP는 Keycloak) nginx 를 덮어쓰기 ``X-Forwarded-*`` 모든 proxied 요청에 대한 ID 헤더."

# libretranslate
msgid "A sidecar `web-app-keycloak` oauth2-proxy authenticates the visitor against Keycloak (OIDC, or LDAP federated through Keycloak) and nginx overwrites the `X-Forwarded-*` identity headers on every proxied request."
msgstr "사이드카 `web-app-keycloak` 오우즈2-proxy는 방문자에게 Keycloak (OIDC, 또는 LDAP는 Keycloak) nginx 를 덮어쓰기 `X-Forwarded-*` 모든 proxied 요청에 대한 ID 헤더."

# libretranslate
msgid "A simple and secure private infrastructure for families and small trusted groups."
msgstr "가족과 작은 신뢰할 수있는 그룹을위한 간단하고 안전한 개인 인프라."

# libretranslate
msgid "A single OpenAI-compatible **LLM gateway** ([LiteLLM Proxy](https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/simple_proxy)) fronts every backend: local `svc-ai-ollama`, a new `svc-ai-lmstudio`, OpenRouter, and any other provider LiteLLM supports. Consumers speak only the gateway `/v1` with a model alias; provider selection and routing are gateway config. This requirement promotes the existing Flowise-local LiteLLM pattern to a shared `svc-ai-litellm` role and makes it the one place backends are declared."
msgstr "단일 OpenAI 호환 **LLM 게이트웨이** ([LiteLLM 프록시](https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/simple_proxy)) 각 백엔드 앞 `svc-ai-ollama`, 새로운 `svc-ai-lmstudio`, OpenRouter 및 다른 공급자 LiteLLM 지원. 소비자는 Gateway만 말합니다. `/v1` 모델 별명으로; 공급자 선택과 여정은 출입구 구성입니다. 이 필요조건은 기존하는 것을 승진시킵니다 Flowise-local LiteLLM 패턴 공유 `svc-ai-litellm` 역할과 한 곳의 백엔드가 선언됩니다."

msgid "A single SPOT for every service-level YAML key that is structurally incompatible with `docker stack deploy` and must therefore be omitted when DEPLOYMENT_MODE == 'swarm'. Currently used for:"
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A single YAML file's parsed root, keyed by absolute path. Every other module routes its YAML reads through here so each file is parsed at most once per process."
msgstr "단일 YAML 파일의 파싱 루트, 절대 경로에 의해 키. 다른 모든 모듈은 YAML이 여기에서 읽을 수 있도록 각 파일이 프로세스 당 한 번에 파싱됩니다."

msgid "A single ``--variant`` (comma-separated, zero-based) selects the matrix rounds a run iterates: ``2`` pins one round, ``0,1,2`` is the runner-split bundle from CI discovery, empty/unset is the full matrix. One value is just a one-element bundle — there is no separate \"variants\" flag — and whether inter-round cleanup runs follows the number of selected rounds, not the flag. Centralising this here keeps init and deploy walking the exact same selection (SPOT)."
